scene intro
  line "Tsayd-tainte: \"The white man draws lines on paper and calls it law. The Kiowa draw lines in the earth with their feet. Which line lasts longer?\""
scene camp
  line "Tsayd-tainte: \"The soldiers think they have conquered us. They do not understand — a people cannot be conquered if they remember who they are.\""
scene camp
  line "Tsayd-tainte: \"In the old days, we measured a man by his horses and his coups. Now they measure us by ration tickets and reservation boundaries.\""
scene mission
  line "Tsayd-tainte: \"I will fight beside you today. But do not ask me to fight my own people.\""
scene mission
  line "Tsayd-tainte: \"The enemy is there. I see them. Wait for my signal.\""
